From 2461b1c00b32c583fbc848a5138dbfc7e8c2c49d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikhail Novosyolov <m.novosyolov@rosa.ru>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 10:52:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] alsa: prefer UCM "HiFi*" like "analog-*"

Node priorities include a small bonus for a few profile names that
ACP generates for classic mixer-path cards: "analog-*" gets +9,
"iec958-*" +8, "pro-*" +500. This keeps outputs backed by a codec
ahead of codec-less ones such as HDMI "stereo-fallback" sinks.

ACP (ALSA Card Profiles, the PulseAudio card handling forked into
PipeWire) also manages UCM cards, but names their device profiles
"<verb>: <device>: <direction>", which never matches those prefixes.
UCM playback nodes stay at the base priority of 1000 and routinely
lose the default sink election to HDMI.

Prefer "HiFi*" like "analog-*": give the HiFi verb the same +9
bonus. The verb name is free-form in the UCM syntax, yet "HiFi" is
the conventional primary playback verb, defined in the public
alsa-lib API (SND_USE_CASE_VERB_HIFI) and ranked topmost in the
PulseAudio/ACP verb priority table.

Co-authored-by: Z.AI GLM
Origin: upstream, https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/pipewire/wireplumber/-/commit/2461b1c00b32c583fbc848a5138dbfc7e8c2c49d
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-13
---
 src/scripts/monitors/alsa.lua | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/scripts/monitors/alsa.lua b/src/scripts/monitors/alsa.lua
index 2a591b2..57632e5 100644
--- a/src/scripts/monitors/alsa.lua
+++ b/src/scripts/monitors/alsa.lua
@@ -390,6 +390,11 @@ function createNode(parent, id, obj_type, factory, properties)
       priority = priority + 9
     elseif profile:find("^iec958%-") then
       priority = priority + 8
+    elseif profile:find("^HiFi.+: sink$") then
+      -- UCM playback profiles are named "<verb>: <device>: sink" and never
+      -- match the ACP prefixes above; give the conventional HiFi verb the
+      -- analog bonus so codec outputs win over e.g. HDMI fallback sinks
+      priority = priority + 9
     end
 
     if dev_props["device.bus"] == "usb" then
